{
  "mn17:0.1": "Middle Discourses 17 ",
  "mn17:0.2": "Jungle Thickets ",
  "mn17:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn17:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn17:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "mn17:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "mn17:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn17:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn17:2.1": "“Mendicants, I will teach you an exposition about jungle thickets. ",
  "mn17:2.2": "Listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "mn17:2.3": "“Yes, sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn17:2.4": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn17:3.1": "“Mendicants, take the case of a mendicant who lives close by a jungle thicket. ",
  "mn17:3.2": "As they do so, their mindfulness does not become established, their mind does not become immersed in samādhi, their defilements do not come to an end, and they do not arrive at the supreme sanctuary from the yoke. ",
  "mn17:3.3": "And the necessities of life that a renunciate requires—robes, almsfood, lodgings, and medicines and supplies for the sick—are hard to come by. ",
  "mn17:3.4": "That mendicant should reflect: ",
  "mn17:3.5": "‘While living close by this jungle thicket, my mindfulness does not become established, my mind does not become immersed in samādhi, my defilements do not come to an end, and I do not arrive at the supreme sanctuary from the yoke. ",
  "mn17:3.6": "And the necessities of life that a renunciate requires—r